# Working in cursor_practice

Practice portfolio, not production. Prefer small, reviewable changes and match
existing patterns in the file you are editing.

## Small slices

One user story per turn (one AC if the story is large). Do not implement
several unrelated stories in one go unless the user asks.

## Product code (`paper-trail/**`)

- Static HTML/CSS/JS only. No framework, bundler, build step, or npm deps.
- One shared stylesheet: `paper-trail/css/styles.css`. No per-page CSS.
- Stage ladder: A static screens, B `localStorage` + JS, C a server. Don't
  skip a stage unless asked.

## The one rule

Nothing written to the log can be edited or deleted — corrections are
appended, timestamps come from a clock, never a form field. If a change
would let someone rewrite history, stop and say so before writing it.

## Naming

Stories are `US-001`, criteria `US-001-AC-1`. Name automated checks after the
AC they cover (`US-002-AC-2`, not `test_form_validation`). Never renumber or
reuse an id — reopen the story instead.
